WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.327
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online TOEFL preparation.

2
00:00:05.627 --> 00:00:08.816
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.116 --> 00:00:16.668
Unit eleven: Writing: Build a Sentence. Today you will arrange scrambled words into a correct, natural sentence.

4
00:00:16.968 --> 00:00:19.550
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:23.768
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.617 --> 00:00:25.618
Scrambled.

7
00:00:26.617 --> 00:00:29.139
Scrambled means mixed up in the wrong order.

8
00:00:29.750 --> 00:00:31.088
The words are scrambled.

9
00:00:31.683 --> 00:00:34.127
Your turn. Say: Scrambled.

10
00:00:36.967 --> 00:00:37.910
Scrambled.

11
00:00:38.650 --> 00:00:39.709
Word order.

12
00:00:40.717 --> 00:00:44.156
Word order means the usual order of words in a sentence.

13
00:00:44.750 --> 00:00:46.703
English has a fixed word order.

14
00:00:47.317 --> 00:00:49.899
Your turn. Say: Word order.

15
00:00:52.733 --> 00:00:53.990
Word order.

16
00:00:54.750 --> 00:00:55.693
Subject.

17
00:00:56.683 --> 00:00:59.287
Subject means the person or thing doing the action.

18
00:00:59.883 --> 00:01:01.535
The subject comes first.

19
00:01:02.150 --> 00:01:04.454
Your turn. Say: Subject.

20
00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:08.243
Subject.

21
00:01:08.983 --> 00:01:09.775
Verb.

22
00:01:10.783 --> 00:01:13.294
Verb means a word for an action or state.

23
00:01:13.883 --> 00:01:15.627
The verb follows the subject.

24
00:01:16.217 --> 00:01:18.614
Your turn. Say: Verb.

25
00:01:21.467 --> 00:01:22.549
Verb.

26
00:01:23.283 --> 00:01:24.157
Object.

27
00:01:25.150 --> 00:01:28.148
Object means the person or thing receiving the action.

28
00:01:28.750 --> 00:01:30.552
The object comes after the verb.

29
00:01:31.150 --> 00:01:33.559
Your turn. Say: Object.

30
00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:37.297
Object.

31
00:01:38.050 --> 00:01:39.156
Auxiliary.

32
00:01:40.150 --> 00:01:43.136
Auxiliary means a helping verb like do or have.

33
00:01:43.750 --> 00:01:45.784
Use an auxiliary in questions.

34
00:01:46.383 --> 00:01:49.221
Your turn. Say: Auxiliary.

35
00:01:52.067 --> 00:01:53.764
Auxiliary.

36
00:01:54.517 --> 00:01:55.645
Question form.

37
00:01:56.650 --> 00:01:59.218
Question form means the word order of a question.

38
00:01:59.817 --> 00:02:01.398
Check the question form.

39
00:02:01.983 --> 00:02:04.938
Your turn. Say: Question form.

40
00:02:07.800 --> 00:02:09.057
Question form.

41
00:02:09.817 --> 00:02:10.969
Punctuation.

42
00:02:11.983 --> 00:02:14.981
Punctuation means marks like commas and full stops.

43
00:02:15.583 --> 00:02:17.432
Add the correct punctuation.

44
00:02:18.017 --> 00:02:21.145
Your turn. Say: Punctuation.

45
00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:25.187
Punctuation.

46
00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:29.755
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:30.617 --> 00:02:32.941
Visal, what is Build a Sentence?

48
00:02:34.050 --> 00:02:43.274
You see a short question or comment from a conversation and a set of scrambled words. You put the words in order to make a correct reply.

49
00:02:44.383 --> 00:02:45.965
What is the best strategy?

50
00:02:47.050 --> 00:02:58.598
Look for the subject and verb first. Then add the object, time and place words. In questions, remember the order: question word, auxiliary, subject, main verb.

51
00:02:59.683 --> 00:03:01.253
What mistakes are common?

52
00:03:02.350 --> 00:03:12.047
Students forget articles and capital letters, or use the wrong word order in embedded questions, such as I don't know where she is, not where is she.

53
00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:14.816
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:15.650 --> 00:03:20.506
Grammar focus: Strategy: subject, verb, object, extra details.

55
00:03:20.806 --> 00:03:22.016
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:22.717 --> 00:03:24.647
She asked where the library was.

57
00:03:25.550 --> 00:03:27.259
Where did you put the keys?

58
00:03:28.200 --> 00:03:35.485
Find the subject and the verb, then build the rest in the usual English order. In questions, use the auxiliary before the subject.

59
00:03:36.250 --> 00:03:40.307
Be careful! Don't say: I put the verb before the subject.

60
00:03:42.267 --> 00:03:44.615
Say: I put the subject before the verb.

61
00:03:44.915 --> 00:03:46.519
Subject, then verb.

62
00:03:47.333 --> 00:03:49.997
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:50.800 --> 00:03:52.219
Putting Words in Order.

64
00:03:52.519 --> 00:03:55.134
The prompt asks: Did you finish the report?

65
00:03:56.133 --> 00:03:59.073
The scrambled words are finished, I, it, yesterday.

66
00:04:00.067 --> 00:04:02.031
Kanha puts I first as the subject.

67
00:04:03.033 --> 00:04:06.322
Then she adds finished it, and yesterday goes last.

68
00:04:07.333 --> 00:04:09.542
The answer is I finished it yesterday.

69
00:04:10.633 --> 00:04:14.809
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:15.650 --> 00:04:17.185
The usual order is blank.

71
00:04:17.485 --> 00:04:23.461
A, object, subject, verb. B, verb, subject, object. C, subject, verb, object.

72
00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:29.673
The answer is C: subject, verb, object.

73
00:04:30.817 --> 00:04:33.432
In a question, the auxiliary comes blank.

74
00:04:33.732 --> 00:04:38.349
A, before the subject. B, after the object. C, at the end.

75
00:04:41.900 --> 00:04:44.364
The answer is A: before the subject.

76
00:04:45.517 --> 00:04:46.669
Which is correct?

77
00:04:46.969 --> 00:04:52.294
A, I don't where she is know.. B, I don't know where she is.. C, I don't know where is she..

78
00:04:55.833 --> 00:04:58.460
The answer is B: I don't know where she is..

79
00:04:59.617 --> 00:05:01.280
What is Kanha's answer?

80
00:05:01.580 --> 00:05:07.462
A, Finished I yesterday it.. B, Yesterday it I finished.. C, I finished it yesterday..

81
00:05:11.000 --> 00:05:13.812
The answer is C: I finished it yesterday..

82
00:05:14.950 --> 00:05:16.764
Which marks should you not forget?

83
00:05:17.064 --> 00:05:21.042
A, capital letters. B, emoji. C, drawings.

84
00:05:24.600 --> 00:05:26.913
The answer is A: capital letters.

85
00:05:28.100 --> 00:05:31.507
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:32.350 --> 00:05:34.884
How do you build a sentence from scrambled words?

87
00:05:43.683 --> 00:05:45.207
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:45.507 --> 00:06:01.432
I find the subject and the verb first, because they form the core of the sentence. Then I add the object and the details of time and place. I check word order, especially in questions, and I add the correct punctuation.

89
00:06:01.732 --> 00:06:03.360
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:06:04.250 --> 00:06:10.629
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and strategy: subject, verb, object, extra details.

91
00:06:10.929 --> 00:06:15.776
Today's value is logical rigor. Follow your reasoning wherever it honestly leads.

92
00:06:16.076 --> 00:06:18.647
See you in Unit twelve. Goodbye!

93
00:06:18.947 --> 00:06:22.226
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

